// Chinese course: every grammar point of the HSK 3.0 grammar syllabus (国际中文教育中文水平等级标准,
// GF 0025-2021, appendix A: 573 points), in the syllabus order, at the syllabus level. Units follow the
// syllabus's own groups (word classes, phrases, fixed patterns, sentence parts, sentence types, aspect,
// questions, emphasis, spoken patterns) within each level; a group with fewer than 3 points at a level
// joins "More grammar at this level", and a group over 12 points is split. `ref` is the point's index
// in the syllabus (HSK 3.0 #1 to #573), so src/core/course/course.test.ts can check full coverage.
// Names, notes and examples are written for Sayfern; the syllabus gives only the points and levels.
// Grammar ids reuse the ids the tutor already records (zh:bi-comparison, zh:chule-hai, ...).
